Breaker has some tie to Native American tribes, as referenced to on the tribal markings on his arms, the feathers, and the style of his armor. Native Americans had great respect for the animal spirits, including the bear. Legends about bears being incredibly good at wrestling come from Breaker Titans' ability to Grapple. {{source|Huntik.com}} Breaker is also closely related to the [[Breaker Cub]] Titan. {{source|TCG:OAL-053|OAL-053}}

Later a Breaker amulet would come into the hands of the [[Organization]] operative, [[Grier]], who would use him in numerous battles against the [[Huntik Foundation]].

Grier invoked Breaker in the [[Huntik Foundation]] library in Venice to attack [[Dante|Dante Vale's]] [[Caliban]]. To give Dante, [[Lok Lambert]], [[Sophie Casterwill]] and [[Santiago]] time to escape, Caliban threw a large shelf on top of Breaker. {{source|The Casterwill Client}}

In the attic of [[Jodis Lore]], Grier invoked Breaker to again fight against Dante's Caliban. With help from [[DeFoe|DeFoe's]] [[Kreutalk]], Breaker was able to defeat Caliban before defeating [[Zhalia Moon|Zhalia Moon's]] [[Kilthane]]. After being distracted by [[Solwing]], Breaker charged at Sophie only to be disorientated by a [[Boltflare]] from Zhalia. When Dante succeeded in invoking Lore's Titan, [[Metagolem]], Breaker was defeated by a single hit from Metagolem. {{source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}}

In the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]], Breaker fought against the Huntik team's Titans, including Caliban, Kilthane and Lok's [[Freelancer]]. Despite gaining the upper hand against the Titans, Breaker was defeated Caliban after being held back by Metagolem. {{source|Into the River of Secrets}} Breaker was later invoked by Grier in the [[Paris Catacombs]] to fight Caliban who punched him to the ground. After recovering Breaker attacked Dante's [[Freelancer]] before being buried in rocks by Dante's [[Raypulse]]. {{source|Divide and Conquer}}

Grier invoked Breaker in the [[Basilisk House]] to fight [[Kilthane]]. After an attack from [[Sabriel]], Breaker and Grier pursued Sophie and Zhalia alongside another [[Suit]] and their [[Mindrone]]. Later, Grier used Breaker to fight and defeat Caliban. Breaker was defeated however when Zhalia bonded with [[King Basilisk]] who turned Breaker to stone. {{source|Absent Heroes}}

In Greece, Grier invoked Breaker as part of DeFoe's plan to ambush the Huntik team and kill Dante. He fought against Zhalia's Kilthane while Dante and his team fled to the shipwreck that they had uncovered. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}}

When Grier and his [[Suits]] took control of [[Sutos Island]], Breaker was invoked to scare any inhabitant who challenged the Organization's rule. Breaker was later used to fight Metagolem and Caliban while Grier and Dante fought one on one. Later, Breaker was again invoked alongside [[Megataur]] as Grier and Dante prepared to fight to the end. However, the battle was stopped when Grier revealed he had come to restore order and peace to Sutos after his father, [[Zan-Sutos]], was killed by a mob. With the two Seekers having resolved their differences, Grier allowed Dante and his team to leave. {{source|Like Father, Unlike Son}}

Breaker became Powerbonded to Grier during a battle in [[the Professor's castle]] in order to save him from asphyxiation at the hands [[Wilder|Wilder's]] [[Grand Façade]], much to the amazement of [[Den Fears]]. Powerbonded Breaker then defeated Grand Façade with his Crushing Grip. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}
